course: dictionary
lesson: 15614
title: Tarzan, a name and a joke
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tarzan with a capital T is a name. It belongs to a made-up character, a boy raised by apes in the African jungle who grows up very strong and swings through the trees on vines. «Tarzan let go of the vine and swung across the river.» The vine and the jungle are the clues that tell you who Tarzan is.
explain: Tarzan with a small t can be an informal, joking word. «My brother lifted the sofa on his own, and Dad laughed, "What a Tarzan!"» A Tarzan means a very strong, muscly man, and people say it as a joke, often when someone is showing off. Check your meaning by swapping in "very strong man" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Capital letters and small letters can change the meaning. When you see Tarzan as a name, think of the story. When you see a tarzan in a sentence about strength, think of a joke. Always read the words around it to decide which one it is.
fact: Tarzan is a made-up character created by the American writer Edgar Rice Burroughs in the novel "Tarzan of the Apes" (1912).
fact: Tarzan is famous for his loud yell and for swinging on vines, and his friend is Jane.
fact: Disney made a cartoon film of Tarzan in 1999.
fact: Informal: "a Tarzan" means a very strong, muscly man, often said as a joke.
fact: Some people today say the old Tarzan books show Africa and Africans in an unfair way.
exercise: «Tarzan swings from vine to vine through the jungle.» Who is Tarzan? | A cartoon dog | A real king of Africa | *A made-up character, a boy raised by apes | A type of jungle fruit
exercise: Ben lifts his heavy bag onto the top shelf, and his brother laughs, "Look at you, Tarzan!" What does Tarzan mean here? | *A very strong, muscly person, said as a joke | A kind of monkey | A person who is afraid of heights | A teacher
exercise: Who created Tarzan in the novel "Tarzan of the Apes"? | Walt Disney | Jane | A jungle guide | *Edgar Rice Burroughs, an American writer
test: In the story, Tarzan is famous for his loud yell and for what? | Cooking in a kitchen | *Swinging on vines | Singing in a choir | Riding a horse across the desert
test: Which sentence uses tarzan as an informal joke? | Tarzan lives in the jungle with apes | The Disney film of Tarzan was made in 1999 | Tarzan is a character in a famous book | *Mum said my brother was a real Tarzan after he carried all the shopping
exam: Which statement about Tarzan is true? | *Tarzan is a made-up character from a novel by Edgar Rice Burroughs | Tarzan is a real person who lived in Africa in 1912 | Tarzan is a city in America | A tarzan is always a kind of fruit
